   (a) attributes the Specification, for example: "AFSP v0.1 Public Review
       Draft, (c) 2026 CiDR Technologies, Inc. D/B/A Primitive";
   (b) includes or links to this license; and
   (c) does not alter the normative text.

3. Modified versions, translations and derivative works. Changes to the
   Specification are governed by the AFSP Governing Body. No one may publish
   a modified version, translation or derivative work of the Specification,
   or present one as AFSP, unless the AFSP Governing Body has authorized it
   in writing. Proposed changes are made through the extension and comment
   process described in CONTRIBUTING.md, and take effect only when the AFSP
   Governing Body approves them and publishes them as part of the
   Specification.

4. Comment and review. Anyone may quote the Specification in comments,
   reviews, implementation notes and extension proposals.

5. Schemas and example code. The schemas, worked examples and example code in
